  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want Réglages › « Bouton + » to **explain its three choices**, so I pick the right one without trying each. (Operator feedback, 2026-11-17.)\n\n### The three behaviours, as the code implements them\n\nFrom `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRModels/Settings/ReplyButtonBehavior.swift` and `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/TopicReaderView.swift:222-223`, at dev-swift after #1018:\n\n| Choice | What the reader button does |\n|---|---|\n| « Répondre comme le forum » (**default** since #1016) | Icon `square.and.pencil`. The composer starts from **HFR's answer page**, as the site's « Répondre » does, with the selected quotes. The topic's draft is kept and the quotes are merged into it. |\n| « Réponse rapide » (legacy's default) | Icon « + ». The composer opens on the **topic's local draft**. The selected quotes **are merged into it** too: unlike the operator's guess, quotes are not ignored. Verify this in the code (the composer's quote merge path) and test it before writing the text. |\n| « Pas d'icône » | No reply button in the reader. Replying stays possible from the message menu: check which entries remain and say so. |\n\n### Scope\n\n1. Under the « Bouton + » picker (`App/SwiftHFR/Settings/SettingsView.swift:154-156`), add a **description of the selected choice** as a section footer or a secondary text under the row. Use the pattern of the operator's decision F on #1014: a description under the control, **no (i) button**. Keep it to one short sentence per choice, in French, matching the table once verified.\n2. If what the code does differs from the doc comment (for instance quick reply ignores quotes), the text follows the **code**. Report the difference on this issue; do not change the behaviour here.\n3. Accessibility: the description is read with the row.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- A test that each `ReplyButtonBehavior` has a non-empty description and that the footer shows the selected one.\n- A test of the quick-reply quote merge, if none exists already, so the sentence is backed by a test.\n- Tests fail without the change.\n\n### Device check (for the #893 general review)\n\nRéglages › Bouton +: the sentence under the picker changes with the choice.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
