   "body": "Verified in the code (dev-swift @ aec0724), as asked; the text follows the code.\n\n| Choice | What the code does |\n|---|---|\n| « Réponse rapide » (`quick`) | Icon « + ». `requestReply()` opens the composer on the topic's draft; with a multi-quote selection, `HFR`'s quotes are fetched (`selectionQuote(answerFormURL:)`) and **merged into the draft** by `QuoteDraftMerger` (`TopicReaderModel+Quote.swift:21-39`, `ReplyComposerModel.swift:147-149`). Quotes are **not** ignored: the operator's guess was wrong, the doc comment was right (LOT-086 difference 3, GAP-083). |\n| « Répondre comme le forum » (`forum`) | **Same `requestReply()`**: nothing in the app reads `replyButton` except `TopicReaderView.replySymbol:221-223` (pencil vs plus) and the hidden case. The table of this issue says the composer « starts from HFR's answer page » for `forum` and not for `quick`: the code does not make that difference (`TopicReaderModel+Quote.swift:21`: « `quick` and `forum` alike »). Only the icon differs. |\n| « Pas d'icône » (`hidden`) | No reply button (`replySymbol` nil). What remains: « Citer » and « Citer ☐ » in the message menu (`quoteHandlers`), and « Citer extrait / gras » in the selection menu; each opens the composer with the quote merged into the draft. No « Répondre » menu entry exists. |\n\nSo the sentences say: quick = draft + selected quotes; forum = same as quick, only the icon differs; hidden = reply from the message menu (« Citer »). Behaviour is not changed here.\n\nIf « Répondre comme le forum » is meant to start from HFR's answer page for real (a different behaviour from « Réponse rapide »), that is a feature that does not exist today (default since #1016 included): it needs its own decision and issue.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
