   "updated_at": "2026-11-17T21:24:31Z",
   "body": "cloud/i970-sonnet, deviation from the acceptance criteria, PR #1064: « a test that the info button is present » has **no test of the button itself**. The tests cover the three sentences (non-empty, distinct, each says what the code does), the default marked, the label's wording, and the quote merge through the reply button. Deleting the `InfoBubbleButton` line from `ReplyButtonRow` would break none of them. A hosted test that finds the button in the accessibility tree and taps it is something I cannot write and run without a Mac. Left to the device check on #893: Réglages › Bouton +, the (i) button is there, a tap opens a bubble (not a sheet) on iPhone with the three choices and the default marked, and VoiceOver reads « À propos du bouton + ».\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
